WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.760
Goals in this inverted pyramid
of sort of a hierarchy.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:08.440
Hi, there Steve Kaufmann here today
and I'm going to talk today about

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.560
goals, goals in language learning.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.160
Uh, remember if you enjoy
these videos, please subscribe.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.290
Um, Click on the bell for notifications.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:20.930
If you follow me on a podcast service,
which I think is a good thing to do,

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.450
because then you can listen, especially
if you're using my videos to improve

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:29.970
your English, you can listen to them
while you're in the car or whatever

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.730
you're doing, but to do leave a review.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:32.570
I do appreciate it.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.890
So why do I want to talk about goals?

00:00:35.629 --> 00:00:41.400
Uh, um, personally, I have the sort
of general interest in learning

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.360
languages which motivates me.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.080
So I don't really focus on any
particular goals, but I, I sort of

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.480
gave the subject some thought, you
know, so much of the time when we're

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.120
learning a language, we have the
feeling that we're not progressing.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.120
We're not getting anywhere.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.950
And so I thought it, it, it is useful.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.150
I kind of looked at what I do
and, and what are the goals that

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.870
I focus on at different stages?

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:07.660
In my language learning, what are,
what sort of is the hierarchy of goals?

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.539
And so that's what I want
to talk about a bit today.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.060
At least my hierarchy of goals, uh,
what I kind of consider to be more

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.979
important at what stage in my learning.

00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:23.100
Uh, and, uh, there are seven of
them and I'm gonna talk about the

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:29.729
seven a day, and then I've been
giving some thought to doing one uh

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.650
video on each of these seven goals.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:35.690
In other words, how do we,
you know, achieve those goals?

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:41.570
How do we use those goals to
improve our, our, uh, ability in

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:42.490
the language that we're learning?

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:49.130
So, first of all, I see these seven
goals as sort of an inverted pyramid,

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.960
uh, where the first one, which I
will start to discuss shortly is

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.040
at the top as a broad sort of line.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.250
Uh, and then the next one comes below it.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:05.730
And so they get sort of narrower
and yet they're expanding sort of

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.610
horizontally, uh, all the time.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.090
Uh, so let me tell you what I mean.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:15.385
So the first goal in language learning
uh, the one that's easiest to sort

00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:21.505
of measure and which stays with you
all the time is acquiring words.

00:02:22.085 --> 00:02:22.465
All right.

00:02:23.725 --> 00:02:28.425
That's why we have at LingQ, we measure
the words you know, uh, we also measure

00:02:28.535 --> 00:02:32.305
phrases or we at least let you save
phrases, but the key measurement is

00:02:32.305 --> 00:02:37.735
the words you know, and, um, certainly
that's what I focus on at the beginning.

00:02:38.515 --> 00:02:42.375
Uh, and I will get into detail
when I do my video on words.

00:02:43.359 --> 00:02:47.780
But that's kind of like the initial,
I often refer to the mechanical rabbit

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:51.700
that you're chasing this thing to try
and, you know, you're running this

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.019
race and you're pursuing the rabbit.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.420
To me the mechanical rabbit is words.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.180
That's the number one goal.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.060
And when you start in the language,
that's what you're trying to do.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:00.460
You're...

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:04.730
one word at a time you're
learning how this language works.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:08.490
So number one goal is
words, acquiring words.

00:03:09.885 --> 00:03:14.265
The second goal on this inverted
pyramid, one level down is

00:03:14.265 --> 00:03:16.505
reading, reading comprehension.

00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:21.795
It's a lot easier to understand
what you read than to understand

00:03:21.795 --> 00:03:22.835
what you're listening to.

00:03:23.255 --> 00:03:28.475
So as you are acquiring words, uh,
you're also developing the ability

00:03:28.655 --> 00:03:32.955
to make sense of what you read, not a
hundred percent, but you're starting

00:03:32.955 --> 00:03:34.475
to make sense of what you read.

00:03:34.775 --> 00:03:38.235
If you're using LingQ, you're looking
words up, you're adding these words

00:03:38.295 --> 00:03:41.505
to your known words total, or to
your words that you have looked

00:03:41.505 --> 00:03:42.825
up that are in your database.

00:03:43.325 --> 00:03:48.725
So the next sort of goal is to increase
the number of words that you are reading,

00:03:48.954 --> 00:03:51.195
something that we also measure at LingQ.

00:03:51.954 --> 00:03:55.005
Then the third goal is
listening comprehension.

00:03:55.584 --> 00:04:00.005
Uh, it it's, I find it
difficult to understand what I

00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:01.965
listen to if I don't read it.

00:04:02.265 --> 00:04:06.915
So that's why in my hierarchy of
goals, I start with acquiring words

00:04:07.055 --> 00:04:11.075
and I wanna see that number go up:
LingQs created, you know, known words

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.380
uh, reading, number of words read.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.940
I wanna see that go up, but
at the same time, I wanna work

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.300
on my listening comprehension.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:24.100
Now to some extent, the listening
comprehension, the learning words, the

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.620
reading is all happening at the same time.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:29.700
But in terms of a goal that
I set for myself initially, I

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:30.980
want that word count to go up.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:34.890
Second of all, I wanna read more
words and I'll get into more detail

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:36.250
when I do a video on reading.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.450
The third thing is to improve
my listening comprehension.

00:04:40.525 --> 00:04:46.385
So those are the first three goals,
the next goal then, and you'll, you'll

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:50.305
sort of realize now that, because I
always talk about input, acquiring

00:04:50.305 --> 00:04:55.424
words, reading, listening, those are
the top three then comes speaking.

00:04:55.844 --> 00:05:00.775
So, uh, as a goal, you know, ultimately at
the end, of course, I wanna able to speak

00:05:00.775 --> 00:05:04.155
well, but initially, that's not my goal.

00:05:04.385 --> 00:05:08.075
Initially my goal is comprehension:
words, reading comprehension,

00:05:08.075 --> 00:05:09.034
listening comprehension.

00:05:09.335 --> 00:05:14.755
And if I have those, a good base in
those, the speaking will be easier for me.

00:05:15.224 --> 00:05:19.635
Then of course I wanna speak as much as
I can, but if I have that solid base in

00:05:19.635 --> 00:05:24.025
the earlier goals, the words, the reading
comprehension, listening comprehension,

00:05:24.455 --> 00:05:25.784
then the speaking is gonna come.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:31.745
Now, after speaking comes grammar
or usage or speaking correctly.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:38.280
So in other words, I don't worry
at all about how correctly I speak

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.960
at an early stage in the language.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.600
My goals initially are input related.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:44.800
Then I'm speaking, speaking with mistakes.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:45.560
It doesn't matter.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:51.720
Then comes a point where I want to
focus in on speaking more correctly.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:55.150
And this comes after struggling to
speak and throwing out the words

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.510
and the phrases that I've acquired.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:00.495
And now I want to work towards
speaking more correctly.

00:06:00.495 --> 00:06:04.615
And when I do my video on how to learn
grammar, I will talk in more detail

00:06:04.625 --> 00:06:10.695
about how we learn grammar and speak more
correctly or more like native speakers.

00:06:11.945 --> 00:06:17.045
So the goals so far have been first goal,
biggest goal, which stays with us, all

00:06:17.045 --> 00:06:18.365
of these, stay with us the whole time:

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:19.770
acquiring words.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.650
Reading second goal:
reading comprehension.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.130
Third is listening comprehension.

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:26.969
Fourth is speaking.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:32.610
Fifth is, uh, grammar learning to,
uh, use the language more correctly.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.570
Then the sixth one is writing.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:39.920
And again, we can start writing
at any time, but, and I, I

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.120
just look at my own experience.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:46.040
I tend not to write a lot, except when
I was in a situation where I needed

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:47.440
to write when I was learning Chinese.

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:49.335
I was on a program.

00:06:49.854 --> 00:06:51.375
I was working for the Canadian government.

00:06:51.695 --> 00:06:55.015
I had to learn to read, excuse me,
to write and to write correctly.

00:06:55.205 --> 00:06:58.854
Similarly, when I was a student in
France, I had, I had to write correctly.

00:06:58.854 --> 00:07:02.614
So there are many situations where
we need to write and write correctly.

00:07:02.875 --> 00:07:09.145
And I will do a video on how we improve
our ability to write and to write uh, you

00:07:09.145 --> 00:07:14.265
know, effectively and, uh, persuasively
and accurately and all these things.

00:07:14.804 --> 00:07:18.465
So that then is the sixth goal is the
writing goal, at least in my hierarchy.

00:07:19.885 --> 00:07:21.784
And the final goal is the culture.

00:07:22.924 --> 00:07:27.304
And, uh, I think at least in my
learning, when I learn a language,

00:07:27.465 --> 00:07:29.815
I learn the language in order
to connect with the culture.

00:07:30.284 --> 00:07:35.710
However, as a goal, It's further down
the list because until I have the reading

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:41.910
comprehension, the listing comprehension,
the words, um, you know, a better sense

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:45.870
of the language, it's difficult to
get into the details of the culture.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:52.070
So again, like so many of these goals, we
can introduce them at any time, but I find

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:56.620
that I'm much more interested in things
that relate to the grammar of the lang...

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.775
or excuse me, that relate to
the, uh,  to the culture of

00:07:59.775 --> 00:08:00.655
the language that I'm learning.

00:08:01.034 --> 00:08:06.534
If I have a better ability to read about
these things comfortably in the language,

00:08:06.755 --> 00:08:13.414
rather than having different aspects of
the culture, uh, festivals or different

00:08:13.414 --> 00:08:17.974
family relationships, having all of this
explained to me, say in English, uh,

00:08:18.315 --> 00:08:21.284
at a point where I don't have a good
understanding of the language, I prefer

00:08:21.385 --> 00:08:25.895
to save that until I can go out and
discover it for myself in the language.

00:08:25.955 --> 00:08:29.815
And so I will do another video
specifically on this seventh goal.

00:08:30.195 --> 00:08:36.334
So all I wanted to do today was to
sort of warn you, let you know that

00:08:36.395 --> 00:08:43.245
I'm going to be doing these seven
videos on the seven goals uh, in

00:08:43.245 --> 00:08:44.765
so far as my learning is concerned.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:50.350
Which are these, uh, goals
in this inverted pyramid of

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:52.310
sort of a hierarchy of goals.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:58.189
The top one is, uh, words, get
getting as many words as you can.

00:08:58.209 --> 00:09:01.150
The second one is developing
your, uh, reading comprehension.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:02.790
The second one.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.710
The third one is developing
your listing comprehension.

00:09:06.079 --> 00:09:08.500
The fourth one is speaking.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:12.905
Uh, the fifth one is working
on your correct usage.

00:09:13.725 --> 00:09:18.545
The sixth one is writing and the
seventh and final one is really

00:09:18.545 --> 00:09:20.865
gaining an appreciation of the culture.

00:09:21.885 --> 00:09:22.865
So there you have it.

00:09:23.245 --> 00:09:26.185
Of course, there's a lot of overlap
and many of these things, it can

00:09:26.185 --> 00:09:30.705
be happening at different stages,
but that is my hierarchy of goals.

00:09:31.125 --> 00:09:32.455
So I hope that was used useful.

00:09:32.705 --> 00:09:33.655
Thank you for listening.

00:09:33.915 --> 00:09:34.455
Bye for now.

